1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,670
You wake up at seven in the morning

2
00:00:01,670 --> 00:00:03,870
and pour yourself a glass of water.

3
00:00:04,030 --> 00:00:05,870
Your roommate walks into the kitchen,

4
00:00:06,310 --> 00:00:07,050
rubs his eyes,

5
00:00:07,370 --> 00:00:07,850
and smiles.

6
00:00:08,530 --> 00:00:08,790
Morning.

7
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:10,530
Did you sleep well,

8
00:00:10,530 --> 00:00:11,130
he asks.

9
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:13,270
Yeah, slept like a rock,

10
00:00:13,270 --> 00:00:14,050
you reply.

11
00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:15,770
And right above your lips,

12
00:00:16,050 --> 00:00:17,670
a bright crimson box flashes:

13
00:00:18,190 --> 00:00:18,450
Lie.

14
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:20,430
Rated eighty-four percent.

15
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:20,990
You freeze.

16
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:22,770
Your roommate looks at the

17
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:24,330
breakfast you made and says,

18
00:00:24,570 --> 00:00:26,650
thanks, this tastes amazing.

19
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:29,350
Floating right above his mouth in bold red letters:

20
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:29,950
Lie.

21
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:32,070
He thinks it is cold and bland.

22
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:33,870
For the next seven days,

23
00:00:34,150 --> 00:00:36,010
every spoken word in your world comes

24
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:37,730
with a verified truth rating.

25
00:00:38,130 --> 00:00:39,610
Green for absolute truth.

26
00:00:40,030 --> 00:00:41,410
Bright crimson for deception.

27
00:00:41,930 --> 00:00:43,150
You think this power will give

28
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:44,490
you the ultimate advantage.

29
00:00:44,990 --> 00:00:47,170
You think you will finally know who to trust.

30
00:00:47,430 --> 00:00:49,150
Instead, by day seven,

31
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:51,450
you will understand the terrifying truth:

32
00:00:51,770 --> 00:00:53,790
Honesty does not save relationships.

33
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:55,230
Kindness does.

34
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:57,250
And polite lies are the only reason

35
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:59,370
society has not burned to the ground.

36
00:01:00,110 --> 00:01:01,350
By noon on day one,

37
00:01:01,590 --> 00:01:03,630
you are sitting in a team meeting at work.

38
00:01:03,870 --> 00:01:06,530
Your manager clicks to the next slide and says,

39
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:08,490
I really appreciate everyone's

40
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:10,110
extra hours on this launch.

41
00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:11,730
Crimson tag: Lie.

42
00:01:12,130 --> 00:01:14,250
He only cares about his quarterly bonus.

43
00:01:14,670 --> 00:01:16,250
A colleague leans over and whispers,

44
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:19,410
don't worry, your presentation was fantastic.

45
00:01:20,010 --> 00:01:21,230
Crimson tag: Lie.

46
00:01:21,590 --> 00:01:23,670
She did not listen to a single word.

47
00:01:24,070 --> 00:01:26,290
Psychologist Robert Feldman discovered that

48
00:01:26,290 --> 00:01:28,250
in an ordinary ten-minute conversation,

49
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:31,190
the average human tells two to three lies.

50
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:33,410
We do not do it because we are monsters.

51
00:01:33,950 --> 00:01:35,690
We do it because radical honesty

52
00:01:35,690 --> 00:01:37,230
is psychological warfare.

53
00:01:37,450 --> 00:01:39,090
Imagine if everyone said,

54
00:01:39,090 --> 00:01:40,890
I am bored of talking to you.

55
00:01:41,050 --> 00:01:42,590
Your new haircut looks terrible.

56
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:45,730
I only invited you because I felt obligated.

57
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:48,410
Civilization survives on tiny white lies

58
00:01:48,410 --> 00:01:50,590
like an engine survives on motor oil.

59
00:01:50,790 --> 00:01:51,770
Without that oil,

60
00:01:52,030 --> 00:01:53,970
human conversation grinds together

61
00:01:53,970 --> 00:01:55,210
until the gears shatter.

62
00:01:55,430 --> 00:01:57,250
By the end of your second day,

63
00:01:57,250 --> 00:01:58,850
you are terrified to speak.

64
00:01:58,850 --> 00:02:01,710
Because every time someone is nice to you,

65
00:02:01,710 --> 00:02:03,570
the glowing red badge tells you:

66
00:02:03,570 --> 00:02:06,030
They are only trying to survive the interaction.

67
00:02:06,782 --> 00:02:07,702
By day four,

68
00:02:07,882 --> 00:02:10,162
the small white lies stop bothering you.

69
00:02:10,362 --> 00:02:13,062
It is the deeper lies that begin to tear you apart.

70
00:02:13,322 --> 00:02:15,302
You meet your closest friend for coffee.

71
00:02:15,662 --> 00:02:18,342
You ask him how he has been doing since his breakup.

72
00:02:18,682 --> 00:02:19,962
He smiles and says,

73
00:02:20,182 --> 00:02:22,482
honestly, I am completely over it.

74
00:02:22,682 --> 00:02:24,142
I feel freer than ever.

75
00:02:24,302 --> 00:02:25,162
Above his chest,

76
00:02:25,382 --> 00:02:26,762
a soft red glow pulses:

77
00:02:27,342 --> 00:02:27,482
Lie.

78
00:02:27,862 --> 00:02:30,162
He cries himself to sleep every night.

79
00:02:30,542 --> 00:02:32,822
Here, the crimson tag is not malice.

80
00:02:33,122 --> 00:02:33,902
It is shame.

81
00:02:34,222 --> 00:02:36,302
Humans lie to hide their bleeding wounds.

82
00:02:36,302 --> 00:02:38,182
We lie so our friends will not

83
00:02:38,182 --> 00:02:40,162
see how fragile we really are.

84
00:02:40,302 --> 00:02:41,762
Then comes the real shock.

85
00:02:42,042 --> 00:02:42,942
You ask him,

86
00:02:43,022 --> 00:02:43,682
are we good?

87
00:02:43,922 --> 00:02:45,142
You felt distant lately.

88
00:02:45,602 --> 00:02:47,522
He pauses, looks at the table,

89
00:02:47,522 --> 00:02:50,262
and says: I was envious of your promotion.

90
00:02:50,742 --> 00:02:53,402
And I hated myself for feeling that way.

91
00:02:53,502 --> 00:02:54,382
Above his words,

92
00:02:54,602 --> 00:02:55,822
there is no red tag.

93
00:02:56,062 --> 00:02:58,302
A soft emerald light illuminates the air:

94
00:02:58,302 --> 00:02:58,867
Truth.

95
00:02:58,867 --> 00:03:00,562
One hundred percent.

96
00:03:00,562 --> 00:03:02,542
It hits you like a physical shock.

97
00:03:02,802 --> 00:03:05,102
Hearing an ugly truth feels ten times more

98
00:03:05,102 --> 00:03:07,002
loving than hearing a beautiful lie.

99
00:03:07,222 --> 00:03:09,322
Because for the first time in your life,

100
00:03:09,562 --> 00:03:11,622
you are meeting a human being without armor.

101
00:03:12,179 --> 00:03:13,919
On the evening of day six,

102
00:03:13,919 --> 00:03:16,799
you walk back to your apartment in complete silence.

103
00:03:16,979 --> 00:03:18,399
You realize that you have spent

104
00:03:18,399 --> 00:03:20,259
five days judging the world.

105
00:03:20,459 --> 00:03:21,759
You analyzed your boss.

106
00:03:22,059 --> 00:03:23,459
You tested your friends.

107
00:03:23,739 --> 00:03:25,779
You graded every stranger on the subway.

108
00:03:26,179 --> 00:03:27,779
So you walk into your bathroom.

109
00:03:28,339 --> 00:03:29,299
You lock the door.

110
00:03:29,299 --> 00:03:31,619
And you look straight into your own reflection.

111
00:03:32,039 --> 00:03:34,119
I am happy with where I am in life,

112
00:03:34,379 --> 00:03:34,819
you whisper.

113
00:03:35,239 --> 00:03:36,739
Crimson flash: Lie.

114
00:03:37,119 --> 00:03:39,439
I do not care what people think of me.

115
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:41,219
Crimson flash: Lie.

116
00:03:41,219 --> 00:03:43,959
I have forgiven everyone who hurt me.

117
00:03:44,079 --> 00:03:45,379
A violent red pulse:

118
00:03:45,719 --> 00:03:45,939
Lie.

119
00:03:46,359 --> 00:03:48,419
The tears start running down your cheeks.

120
00:03:48,739 --> 00:03:50,799
The most dangerous deceiver in your life

121
00:03:50,799 --> 00:03:52,719
was never your coworker or your partner.

122
00:03:53,079 --> 00:03:53,799
It was you.

123
00:03:53,999 --> 00:03:56,579
We tell ourselves comfortable fairy tales so

124
00:03:56,579 --> 00:03:58,819
we do not have to face our fear of failure,

125
00:03:59,179 --> 00:04:00,899
our grief, and our loneliness.

126
00:04:01,479 --> 00:04:03,699
You stare into the mirror and finally say the

127
00:04:03,699 --> 00:04:06,019
one thing you have avoided for ten years:

128
00:04:06,159 --> 00:04:07,999
I am terrified of being alone.

129
00:04:08,139 --> 00:04:09,859
And I am trying my best.

130
00:04:09,859 --> 00:04:11,479
For the first time all week,

131
00:04:11,779 --> 00:04:12,779
the crimson vanishes.

132
00:04:13,259 --> 00:04:15,739
A deep, tranquil green envelops the glass:

133
00:04:16,159 --> 00:04:16,479
Truth.

134
00:04:16,879 --> 00:04:17,499
Absolute.

135
00:04:18,021 --> 00:04:20,041
Midnight arrives on the seventh day.

136
00:04:20,261 --> 00:04:22,821
The glowing tags fade into the quiet night air.

137
00:04:22,941 --> 00:04:24,541
Over the last six weeks,

138
00:04:24,801 --> 00:04:27,281
you have experienced every impossible power:

139
00:04:27,501 --> 00:04:29,261
You saw the salaries of every neighbor

140
00:04:29,261 --> 00:04:31,181
and realized wealth buys comfort,

141
00:04:31,601 --> 00:04:32,221
not peace.

142
00:04:32,501 --> 00:04:34,221
You saw the karma scores and learned

143
00:04:34,221 --> 00:04:36,041
that morality is an inward discipline,

144
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:37,621
not a public spectacle.

145
00:04:38,001 --> 00:04:40,341
You heard what people whispered behind your back

146
00:04:40,341 --> 00:04:42,581
and found the freedom of not needing applause.

147
00:04:42,581 --> 00:04:44,721
You tasted infinite save points and

148
00:04:44,721 --> 00:04:46,481
discovered that life's beauty exists

149
00:04:46,481 --> 00:04:48,601
only because mistakes are permanent.

150
00:04:48,961 --> 00:04:51,081
You saw the countdown clocks of mortality

151
00:04:51,081 --> 00:04:52,961
and learned that our limited time is

152
00:04:52,961 --> 00:04:54,561
what makes every moment sacred.

153
00:04:54,941 --> 00:04:56,981
And now, seeing every lie has

154
00:04:56,981 --> 00:04:58,421
taught you the ultimate lesson:

155
00:04:58,701 --> 00:05:00,341
Truth without empathy is cruelty.

156
00:05:00,701 --> 00:05:02,241
And honesty without vulnerability

157
00:05:02,241 --> 00:05:03,801
is just another weapon.

158
00:05:04,061 --> 00:05:06,301
You step outside onto the morning sidewalk.

159
00:05:06,761 --> 00:05:08,961
The barista hands you your cup and says,

160
00:05:09,021 --> 00:05:10,381
have a wonderful day.

161
00:05:10,381 --> 00:05:11,801
There is no green tag.

162
00:05:12,141 --> 00:05:13,221
There is no red tag.

163
00:05:13,361 --> 00:05:15,601
Just two strangers on a spinning rock,

164
00:05:15,601 --> 00:05:17,621
trying to be kind to each other.

165
00:05:17,901 --> 00:05:19,141
You smile back at her,

166
00:05:19,321 --> 00:05:20,721
take a sip of hot coffee,

167
00:05:20,721 --> 00:05:22,641
and whisper: Thank you.

168
00:05:22,861 --> 00:05:23,741
And this time,

169
00:05:23,921 --> 00:05:24,701
in your heart,

170
00:05:24,921 --> 00:05:26,641
you know it is the absolute truth.
